district":"Dindigul","address":"Soundram Nagar, Gandhigram Post, Dindigul District - 624302, Tamil Nadu, India","mapLink":"https://maps.google.com/maps?q=The+Gandhigram+Institute+of+Rural+Health+Family+Welfare+Trust+Dindigul","mapQuery":"The+Gandhigram+Institute+of+Rural+Health+Family+Welfare+Trust+Dindigul","website":"https://girhfwt.org/courses/","phone":"+91 451 2999923","email":"mailto:girhfwtdgl@rediffmail.com","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Gandhigram-Institute-of-Rural-Health-and-Family-Welfare-Trust-Dindigul-collegeshine.webp","videoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/OPRJFVTD-KE?si=OqPyWx7n73Etefza&amp;start=13","affiliation":"Diploma in Medical Laboratory Technology (DMLT) recognized by Government of Tamil Nadu; PG Diploma in Health Promotion and Education (PGDHPE) affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University, Chennai; autonomous body under Ministry of Health & Family Welfare, Govt. of India","accreditation":["Autonomous Body under Ministry of Health & Family Welfare, Govt. of India","DMLT Recognized by Government of Tamil Nadu","PGDHPE Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University","Curriculum for Health Visitors Course Approved by Indian Nursing Council (INC), New Delhi","Houses a Population Research Centre (PRC) — One of 18 PRCs in India"],"about":"The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family Welfare Trust (GIRH&FWT) was established in 1964 by Dr. T.S. Soundram, with support from the Government of Tamil Nadu, the Government of India, and the Ford Foundation. It functions today as an autonomous body under the Ministry of Health & Family Welfare, Government of India, with the objective of promoting the implementation of National Health and Family Welfare programmes in rural areas through training, research, and community outreach.\\n\\nThe institute offers three pioneer training courses: the Diploma in Medical Laboratory Technology (DMLT), a 2-year, 30-seat programme recognized by the Government of Tamil Nadu; the Post Graduate Diploma in Health Promotion and Education (PGDHPE), a 12-month, 30-seat programme affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University, Chennai; and the Health Visitors Course, a 6-month promotional training programme for registered ANM/MPHW(F) health workers, with curriculum approved by the Indian Nursing Council (INC), New Delhi. The institute also houses a Population Research Centre (PRC) — one of 18 PRCs operating in India — which has been conducting research in maternal and child health, fertility, mortality, family planning, and rural health since 1959, alongside its Health & Family Welfare Training Centre (HFWTC), Department of Health Promotion and Education (DHPE), and Rural Health Training and Technology Institute (RHTTI) units.","highlights":["Established 1964 — Autonomous Body, Govt. of India","DMLT — 2-Year Diploma, 30 Seats, Govt. of Tamil Nadu Recognized","PGDHPE — Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University","Health Visitors Course — INC-Approved Curriculum for ANM/MPHW(F)","Houses Population Research Centre (PRC) — One of 18 in India","Multiple Specialized Units: HFWTC, DHPE, RHTTI, Central Unit","60+ Years of Rural Health & Family Welfare Training","Strong Community Interface — Health Camps & Outreach Programmes"],"departments":[{"name":"Diploma in Medical Laboratory Technology (DMLT)","level":"Diploma"},{"name":"PG Diploma in Health Promotion and Education (PGDHPE)","level":"PG"},{"name":"Health Visitors Course (Promotional Training for ANM/MPHW-F)","level":"UG"}],"facilities":[{"icon":"ti-wifi","name":"Institute Network"},{"icon":"ti-books","name":"Institute Library"},{"icon":"ti-flask","name":"Medical Laboratory Technology Labs"},{"icon":"ti-home","name":"Hostel Facility"},{"icon":"ti-bus","name":"Transport Facility"},{"icon":"ti-heartbeat","name":"Health & Family Welfare Training Centre (HFWTC)"},{"icon":"ti-crown","name":"Population Research Centre (PRC)"},{"icon":"ti-heart","name":"Rural Health Training & Technology Institute (RHTTI)"},{"icon":"ti-trophy","name":"Sports & Recreation"},{"icon":"ti-microphone","name":"Department of Health Promotion & Education (DHPE)"},{"icon":"ti-cpu","name":"Central Unit"},{"icon":"ti-medall","name":"Kshamta Kendra (Special Programme)"}],"placementRate":70,"avgPackage":"₹2 LPA","highestPackage":"₹4 LPA","placementYear":null,"admissionProcess":[{"title":"Meet Eligibility Criteria","desc":"For DMLT: pass in HSC with Physics, Chemistry, Botany/Zoology or Biology (age 17-32, 37 for SC/ST). For PGDHPE: a Master''s degree with 1 year community-work experience, or a Bachelor''s degree with 2 years community/public-health experience."},{"title":"Download Prospectus & Application","desc":"Download the relevant course prospectus and application form from the official website."},{"title":"Submit Application","desc":"Complete and submit the application form along with required documents before the deadline."},{"title":"Merit-Based Selection","desc":"Seats are allotted based on merit and eligibility as per institute norms (30 seats each for DMLT and PGDHPE)."},{"title":"Reporting & Enrollment","desc":"Report to the institute with original documents to confirm admission."}],"scholarships":[],"events":["Health Camps","Community Outreach Programmes","Sports Meet","Cultural Events","Training Programmes (Statistical/Technical)"],"distanceInfo":{"airport":"75 km (Madurai)","railway":"12 km (Dindigul Junction)","bustand":"10 km","metro":"N/A","hospital":"On Campus (HFWTC)"},"hostelFeatures":["Hostel Facility Available","Mess Facility"],"technicalClubs":["Medical Laboratory Technology Skill Club","Public Health Research Club"],"culturalClubs":["Cultural Events Committee"],"communityService":["Health Camps in Rural Areas","Reproductive & Child Health Research (via PRC)","Family Planning Awareness Programmes","Community Outreach & Public Health Education"]}'),
