ucation Institution"],"about":"IRT Polytechnic College, Bargur is a technical education institution established by the Institute of Road Transport, Taramani, Chennai. The college was started in 1992-1993 with the objective of providing technical education, particularly to the wards of State Transport Corporation employees. The institution initially functioned from the Government Polytechnic College campus at Krishnagiri before moving to its permanent campus at Orappam on the Chennai-Bangalore National Highway.\\n\\nThe college is affiliated to the Directorate of Technical Education, Tamil Nadu and offers three-year diploma programmes in Computer Engineering, Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Electronics and Communication Engineering and Mechanical Engineering. The institution provides theory and practical-oriented technical education through engineering laboratories, workshops, computer facilities and technical training.\\n\\nThe campus is spread over approximately 9.17 acres and provides laboratory, library, classroom, workshop and student-support infrastructure. The institution has a long history of technical education and is operated under the Institute of Road Transport associated with the State Transport Department, Government of Tamil Nadu.","highlights":["Established in 1992","Institute of Road Transport Polytechnic College","Located on Chennai-Bangalore National Highway","Approx. 9.17-Acre Campus","Affiliated to Directorate of Technical Education, Tamil Nadu","Four Diploma Engineering Programmes","Three-Year Full-Time Diploma Courses","Computer Engineering","Electrical & Electronics Engineering","Electronics & Communication Engineering","Mechanical Engineering","Well-Equipped Engineering Laboratories","Workshops & Practical Training","Central Library","Technical Skill Development","Industry-Oriented Education"],"departments":[{"name":"Diploma in Computer Engineering","level":"Diploma"},{"name":"Diploma in Electrical and Electronics Engineering","level"