fcrithalainayar/","phone":"9443724842","email":"mailto:deanfcrithalainayeru@tnfu.ac.in","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/fisheries-college-and-research-institute-thoothukudi.webp","videoUrl":"","affiliation":"Tamil Nadu Dr.J.Jayalalithaa Fisheries University (TNJFU)","accreditation":["Constituent College of Tamil Nadu Dr.J.Jayalalithaa Fisheries University","Government of Tamil Nadu Institution","UGC Recognized University System","ICAR-Based Fisheries Education Framework","State Fisheries University Institution"],"about":"Dr. M.G.R. Fisheries College and Research Institute, Thalainayeru is a constituent fisheries education and research institution of Tamil Nadu Dr.J.Jayalalithaa Fisheries University. The college was established in 2017 at Thalainayeru in Nagapattinam district with the objective of developing skilled manpower in fisheries science, aquaculture, fisheries resource management and allied sectors.\\n\\nThe institute offers the Bachelor of Fisheries Science (B.F.Sc.) programme and supports postgraduate and doctoral teaching and research in fisheries-related disciplines. Its academic activities cover aquaculture, fisheries biology and resource management, fish processing technology, fishing technology and fisheries engineering, aquatic environment management, fisheries extension and allied areas.\\n\\nThe institution benefits from the fisheries resources of the Nagapattinam coastal region. More than 1,000 active shrimp farms around Thalainayeru provide opportunities for practical exposure, while nearby Muthupet mangrove ecosystems and coastal fisheries resources support field-based education and research.\\n\\nThe college promotes practical learning, fisheries research, aquaculture entrepreneurship, extension activities and community-oriented fisheries development. Research activities include marine fishery resource assessment, microplastic and marine-debris studies, aquaculture, fish biology, fishing-gear technology and fisherie