onal Institute of Aquaculture Technology (PPIAT), Muttukadu is a vocational education institute functioning under Tamil Nadu Dr. J. Jayalalithaa Fisheries University through its Directorate of Incubation and Vocational Training in Aquaculture (DIVA). The institute is supported by funding from the National Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development (NABARD) and was established to produce skilled second-level technical personnel for the aquaculture and fisheries sector.\\n\\nThe institute offered a one-year Diploma in Industrial Aquaculture Technology from 2018 and began the three-year Bachelor of Vocation (B.Voc.) in Industrial Aquaculture from 2019 onwards. The programme follows a progressive vocational structure with Diploma, Advanced Diploma and Degree awards at the end of the first, second and third years respectively.\\n\\nThe curriculum provides intensive practical training in shrimp farming, shrimp seed production and hatchery management, shrimp nutrition, disease and health management, water and soil quality, ornamental fish culture, live feed organisms, freshwater aquaculture, marine and brackishwater aquaculture, integrated aquaculture, fish seed production, economics, banking, marketing, fish processing and value addition. Students also complete extended internships and field training.","highlights":["Established in 2019","Government Fisheries Vocational Institute","Constituent Unit of TNJFU","NABARD Funded Initiative","Three-Year B.Voc. in Industrial Aquaculture","One-Year Diploma Stage","Two-Year Advanced Diploma Stage","Three-Year Degree Stage","Shrimp Farming Training","Shrimp Hatchery Management","Freshwater Aquaculture","Marine & Brackishwater Aquaculture","Ornamental Fish Culture","Fish Seed Production","Fish Nutrition & Feed Management","Aquatic Disease & Health Management","Water & Soil Quality Management","Fish Processing & Value Addition","Aquaculture Entrepreneurship","Industry Internship Programme"],"departments":[{"name":"B.Voc. - Industrial 