adu Dr. J. Jayalalithaa Music and Fine Arts University","Under Tamil Nadu Department of Art and Culture"],"about":"Tamil Nadu Government Music College, Madurai was established in 1979 under the Government of Tamil Nadu with the objective of providing systematic education and training in music, dance and traditional performing arts. The institution is located at Pasumalai in Madurai and serves students interested in classical music, instrumental music, Bharathanatyam and traditional folk arts.\\n\\nThe college is affiliated with The Tamil Nadu Dr. J. Jayalalithaa Music and Fine Arts University, Chennai. It offers undergraduate degree programmes and diploma programmes covering vocal music, Veena, Violin, Flute, Nadaswaram, Thavil, Mridangam, Bharathanatyam and Folk Arts. Students receive practical training through performances, cultural programmes, competitions and other performing-arts activities.","highlights":["Established in 1979","Government Music College in Madurai","Located at Pasumalai, Madurai","Affiliated to Tamil Nadu Dr. J. Jayalalithaa Music and Fine Arts University","Three-Year Undergraduate Degree Programmes","Three-Year Diploma Programmes","One-Year Diploma in Music Teaching","Training in Carnatic Vocal Music","Training in Traditional Musical Instruments","Bharathanatyam Training","Folk Arts Training","Annual Music and Cultural Activities"],"departments":[{"name":"B.A. Music - Vocal","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.A. Music - Bharathanatyam","level":"UG"},{"name":"Diploma in Vocal","level":"Diploma"},{"name":"Diploma in Veena","level":"Diploma"},{"name":"Diploma in Violin","level":"Diploma"},{"name":"Diploma in Flute","level":"Diploma"},{"name":"Diploma in Nadaswaram","level":"Diploma"},{"name":"Diploma in Thavil","level":"Diploma"},{"name":"Diploma in Mridangam","level":"Diploma"},{"name":"Diploma in Bharathanatyam","level":"Diploma"},{"name":"Diploma in Folk Arts","level":"Diploma"},{"name":"Diploma in Music Teaching","level":"Diploma"},{"name":"Certificate / Short-Term Music Training","level":"UG"}],"facilities":[{"icon":"ti-microphone","name":"Music Practice Rooms"},{"icon":"ti-music","name":"Vocal Music Training Facility"},{"icon":"ti-music-alt","name":"Instrumental Music Practice Facility"},{"icon":"ti-book","name":"Central Library"},{"icon":"ti-blackboard","name":"Classrooms"},{"icon":"ti-microphone-alt","name":"Performance Hall"},{"icon":"ti-calendar","name":"Cultural Activity Centre"},{"icon":"ti-trophy","name":"Sports Facilities"},{"icon":"ti-home","name":"Student Accommodation"},{"icon":"ti-user","name":"Student Welfare Support"},{"icon":"ti-world","name":"Cultural Outreach Activities"},{"icon":"ti-camera","name":"Audio-Visual Learning Facility"}],"placementRate":72,"avgPackage":"₹2.4 LPA","highestPackage":"₹4.8 LPA","placementYear":null,"admissionProcess":[{"title":"Check Admission Notification","desc":"Candidates should check the Tamil Nadu Department of Art and Culture admission notification for the relevant academic year."},{"title":"Choose the Programme","desc":"Students can select an undergraduate degree or diploma programme according to their educational qualification and area of interest."},{"title":"Verify Eligibility","desc":"UG applicants generally require Higher Secondary or equivalent qualification, while diploma applicants generally require the prescribed secondary-level qualification."},{"title":"Submit Application","desc":"Candidates submit the application form together with the required educational and identity documents."},{"title":"Selection and Admission","desc":"Eligible candidates complete the selection, fee payment and admission formalities according to the government college admission procedure."}],"scholarships":["Government Scholarship","Post-Matric Scholarship","BC / MBC Scholarship","SC / ST Scholarship","First Graduate Scholarship","Minority Scholarship","Merit-Based Student Assistance","Government Welfare Scholarship","Free Bus Pass for Eligible Students","Financial Assistance fo